title: Karen_Encounter
---
// $sanity represents the player's sanity (0-100).
// Ideally this should be declared ONCE in a separate file (e.g. Variables.yarn),
// but we're leaving it here for now to test quickly.
<<declare $sanity = 100 as number>>

Karen: Excuse me?! This is NOT what I ordered!
Karen: I've been waiting ten minutes and nobody has properly helped me.

-> Apologize and offer an immediate exchange
    Player: I'm so sorry, ma'am. Let me exchange the product right now, free of charge.
    <<set $sanity = $sanity - 5>>
    <<refresh_sanity>>
    Karen: Well... I suppose that's fine. Faster next time, though.
    <<jump Karen_Resolved>>

-> Explain the store's policy calmly
    Player: I understand your frustration, but this is our return policy.
    <<if $sanity <= 50>>
        Karen: HOW DARE YOU question me?! I want to speak to your manager RIGHT NOW!
        <<set $sanity = $sanity - 20>>
        <<refresh_sanity>>
        <<jump Karen_Escalate>>
    <<else>>
        Karen: Hmph. Fine, I understand. But don't let it happen again.
        <<set $sanity = $sanity - 10>>
        <<refresh_sanity>>
        <<jump Karen_Resolved>>
    <<endif>>

-> Ignore her and keep working
    <<set $sanity = $sanity - 25>>
    <<refresh_sanity>>
    Karen: I'm not leaving until someone helps me properly!
    <<jump Karen_Escalate>>

===

title: Karen_Resolved
---
Karen: Thanks for your help. That wasn't so hard, was it?
<<karen_leave>>
===

title: Karen_Escalate
---
Karen: This is UNACCEPTABLE! I'm leaving a one-star review!

<<if $sanity <= 30>>
    Player: ...
    <<game_over>>
<<else>>
    Karen: Whatever. Not worth my time.
    <<karen_leave>>
<<endif>>
===
